  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `setup_align::verified_kind` now accepts 2D Offset, Trace and Engrave in a setup that holds the part turned. The refusal text names them.\n- The three kinds take their region from `job::region_for_job`. Face, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive use the same door. It reads the part material, the heights and the picks in the setup frame. No new transform is added.\n- The other kinds keep the refusal by name. `docs/decisions/2276-aligned-setup-kinds.md` gives the reason for each kind.\n- `setup_align.rs` and `opframe_picks.rs` used 2D Offset as the example of an unverified kind. They now use Circular.\n\n## Readings\n\n- New suite `crates/app/tests/setup_align_2d_kinds.rs`. It turns an L prism 90 degrees about X, then 90 degrees about Z (two axes, typed angles about the part centre).\n- For each kind, the turned document and the document with the turn baked into the mesh give the same moves (to 1e-6) and the same posted program.\n- Each turned and baked path has no post-blocking warning, and the stock simulation finds no gouge.\n- The part as modelled gives a different path. A generator that reads the model frame fails the test.\n- The bottom height is `TopOfModel - 11`, so the height read is in the setup frame too.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `turned_offset2d_cuts_like_the_baked_part`\n- `turned_trace_cuts_like_the_baked_part`\n- `turned_engrave_cuts_like_the_baked_part`\n- `kinds_without_proof_stay_refused_in_a_turned_setup`\n\nAlso run green: `setup_align` (10), `opframe_picks` (4), `setup_align_2d_area` (5), `setup_align_3d` (6). Clippy `-D warnings` on `camcraft-app` lib and the touched test targets is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Trace and Engrave with a picked chain as the source. The tests use the whole model. The picks go through `selection_geometry_in`, which #2210 and #1736 already pin.\n- 2D Offset with area controls in the turned setup.\n- The quick tier of each crate (targeted tests only).\n\n## Kinds that stay refused (partial fix)\n\nSlot, Trochoidal Slot, Circular, 2D Chamfer, Drill, Bore, Thread, Deburr, Probe, the 5-axis and rotary kinds, and the non-mill kinds. The issue comment lists them with the reasons.\n\nThe verify check and the post gate do not change.\n\nChangelog: A setup that holds the part turned now generates 2D Offset, Trace and Engrave operations.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #2276\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
